bjectives but  there's nothing telling you about the  specifics of an area the lack of  mini-map allows you to see the trees in  the forest so to speak you can focus on  details in the world without distraction  and you can actively appreciate the  stunning beauty of the natural  environment and pay full attention to  the intricate interior details in the  homes and businesses you visit the new  freeform flow sits comfortably while  with the most celebrated aspect of the  Far Cry series the capacity for you to  engage with the game's complex in your  own way seeing what kinds of chance  knives you stumble into and attaining  those water-cooler tales about what  happens next  [Music]  there's also thankfully less of an  emphasis on hunting selling animal skins  is the most lucrative way to earn money  for weapons and vehicles but the series  is finally past the point of needing to  hunt specific creatures for the purposes  of crafting upgrades another fantastic  change involves the affirmation  specialists and the more generic guns  for hire they allow you to command the  unique skills of one of many support  buddies adding another fun and dynamic  element to your toolkit specialists  provide a variety of options from the  humans that lay down covering fire with  different weapons and vehicles to the  animals who can assist you in marking  enemies and stealth takedowns they're  fantastic assets you can complement your  skillset or fill in a necessary gap you  might recruit torture to Archer just to  give you a sound and attack option all  tell the helicopter pilot Adelaide to  fly in and provide suppressing fire and  a distraction  Herk is also back for better or worse  the AI that drives support characters  sometimes makes poor decisions that puts  them in harm's away but in lieu of a  co-op partner specialists help bolster  the series's propensity for emergent  fist-pumping Hellyeah moments  and that's what 5x5 is all about fluid  and dynamic engagements that act a